   "stem": {
      "text": "The function f is defined by f(x) = (x + 21) / (x^2 + 4x + 3) for x < 3 and f(x) = 3 / (6 - x) for x >= 3. Consider the largest interval that contains x = 0 and on which f is continuous. What is the sum of the integers in that interval?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 15
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "For x < 3 the denominator x^2 + 4x + 3 = (x + 1)(x + 3) is zero at x = -3 and x = -1, and for x >= 3 the denominator 6 - x is zero at x = 6, so f is undefined at -3, -1 and 6.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
