               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Each rule is a rational function, continuous on its domain. At the join, the left rule approaches 24 / 24 = 1 and f(3) = 3 / 3 = 1, so f is continuous at x = 3 and on (-infinity, -3) U (-3, -1) U (-1, 6) U (6, infinity).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            3,
            [
               "Subtract",
               6,
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece that contains x = 0 is (-1, 6), open at both ends. Its integers are 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            0,
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4,
            5
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The sum of those integers is 15.",
